<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan weekly forex reserves up at $1.765 bln.</title>
<headline>Pakistan weekly forex reserves up at $1.765 bln.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's foreign exchange reserves rose to $1.765 billion on May 10, from $1.552 billion a week earlier, but were lower against $2.280 billion on May 9, 1996, the State Bank of Pakistan said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Pakistan's weekly foreign exchange holdings position:</p>
<p>    (MLN DLRS)		MAY 10     MAY 3	MAY 9, 1996</p>
<p> TOTAL			 1,765	 1,552	  2,280</p>
<p> Forex in Pakistan	   651	   541	  1,399</p>
<p> Forex outside Pakistan    438	   325	    181</p>
<p> Gold coins and bullion    673	   674	    697</p>
<p> Special Drawing Rights	3	    12		3</p>
<p>			-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
